# Voice Typing

Whisper-based voice dictation for Linux/Wayland and macOS.

## Install (Linux/Sway/Wayland)

$ sudo pacman -S wtype
$ uv tool install .

Bind `whisper-dictation-toggle` to a key in your Sway config:

    bindsym XF86Favorites exec whisper-dictation-toggle

## Install (macOS)

$ uv tool install .

On first run macOS prompts for Microphone access (allow it) and for
permission to control "System Events" so the daemon can paste typed
text (allow it). If keystrokes don't appear, open
**System Settings → Privacy & Security → Accessibility** and enable
the daemon binary at `~/.local/bin/whisper-dictation-daemon`.

Bind a hotkey via Hammerspoon (`~/.hammerspoon/init.lua`):

    hs.hotkey.bind({"cmd", "alt"}, "space", function()
        hs.execute(os.getenv("HOME") .. "/.local/bin/whisper-dictation-toggle")
    end)

## Usage

- First press: loads model (yellow status), then starts recording (red status)
- Second press: stops recording, transcribes, types result
- Subsequent presses: instant toggle (model stays loaded)

## How it works

- `whisper-dictation-daemon`: background process that keeps the Whisper model in VRAM
- `whisper-dictation-toggle`: starts daemon if needed, toggles recording via signal

The daemon stays running after first use for instant recording on subsequent toggles.
It auto-shuts down after 15 minutes idle to free VRAM.

## Stop daemon manually

$ pkill -f whisper-dictation-daemon
